# Original repository nomination prerequisite

The version-2 service executes a new authored repository validation-action
procedure in the actual native signed TEST interpreter. It nominates the exact
current original scorer request; it does not execute tests, declare a repaired
candidate, promote a procedure or authorize publication. It is separate from
the retained arithmetic procedure and certificate.

Thirteen bounded fresh processes passed: four explicit warm-prime original
bases, eight four-family/two-configuration controls, and one exact retained
native Requests parent wire fixture. All used corpus v3 and the strict curator
endpoint declaration v4. The native verifier, issuer and certificate verifier
admitted each TEST-only certificate; all 65 original operation dispatches
completed. Independent audit re-read source, reconstructed all eight evidence
payloads for each case, checked retained query→authority→invocation→action and
emitted receipts, and passed 41 source/request/native tamper controls.

The authored IR includes explicit native test and proof contract IDs for
nomination. Evidence is bounded to exact current public request transport and
authority: an exhaustive 256-row Boolean binding model, exact graph/resource
checks, independently checked scorer projection, changed-binding adversarial
cases and fresh disjoint request namespaces. Its held-out/shadow partitions
are request-namespace controls over the same original source. They establish
neither unseen-task transfer nor source/test truth. Original visible/hidden
tests, objective cases and API configuration controls still require actual
curator execution. The memory reservation is trusted local immutable-input
custody, not hostile-Python process isolation.

All 13 processes exited zero within the prospective 120-second bounds. Their
complete enclosing durations total **21.250885860 seconds**. The qualification
driver measured **22.390933624 seconds**, including profile/key/request
preparation, subprocesses and aggregation after its initial imports; initial
driver startup/imports are outside that measurement. The independent audit
took **6.570655999 seconds**. Service-internal time totals 18.860313325 seconds
and is nested within the process total: actual evidence production 5.185454757,
independent evidence reexecution 5.696616416, current-source observation
0.532181212, initial guards 3.111525972, final guards 3.610027136, native
construction 0.011340497, verifier 0.065137701, issuance/reverification
0.096549010, certificate admission 0.002549501 and native preparation/execution
0.349925120 seconds. Do not sum nested values again. These are real measured
preparation costs, not saved work.

The profile pins 10,725 code/input paths. Every worker reports 31 actually loaded
native/service/helper source paths, all matching the freeze; exact package
roots are included. Standard-library and unrelated host imports are outside
that observed-source manifest. The caller must include complete process
startup in its ledger cost and preserve the current profile/environment pins.

The service accepts the actual `sha256:<64hex>` native Kit parent form and
rejects malformed, cross-trajectory and action-substituted descriptors. A
well-formed descriptor still does not establish that the parent is current:
the audit explicitly retains that accepted nomination boundary, and actual
caller pointer reading/CAS remains outside the service. The real Requests
fixture demonstrates wire compatibility only, without transferring Requests
publication authority to an original repository task.

Both cold and warm invocations repeat evidence and signing. No cross-process
procedure/checkpoint reuse, CALL reuse, production authority, repair success
or token savings is claimed. This closes the executable signed nomination
prerequisite for the original controller; the broader E04/E05 reuse layer is
still open. [API.md](API.md) gives the runnable caller contract.

The earlier `native_profiles/v1`, eight successful native processes and
30-control audit remain unchanged. They used the superseded cold endpoint and
null parents; they do not qualify the corrected endpoint, native parent
codec or warm priming. Two initial authored hook profiles also remain retained.
Version 2 preserved pass, setup failure, CALL failure and teardown failure
against baseline, and rejected changed request bytes/unqualified reuse before
CALL: 10 processes, 2.167776591 seconds total, zero reused calls. Its 32-module
observation list covers native submodules but omits the two executing package
root names; both root source files are nevertheless covered by its full source
freeze. The curator's positive successor must include those root imports and
qualify its separate exact child launcher before any original-suite reuse.
